This is a MATLAB research code for solving the incompressible Navier-Stokes (INS) equations in 2D. Here's what it does:

Core purpose: Numerically simulate viscous, incompressible fluid flow using a pressure-Poisson projection approach on structured grids.

Time integration schemes (selectable via -ts=):
- ab2 — 2nd-order Adams-Bashforth (explicit)
- pc2 — 2nd-order predictor-corrector
- im2 — 2nd-order implicit (Crank-Nicolson style)

Grid support:
- Cartesian, curvilinear (annulus, rectangle, general mapped grids)
- Periodic, Dirichlet, Neumann, slip-wall, inflow/outflow boundary conditions

Test cases & validation:
- Taylor-Green vortex (manufactured solution for convergence testing)
- Poiseuille flow (exact solution)
- Trigonometric/polynomial manufactured solutions for grid convergence studies
- Kelvin-Helmholtz shear flow instability (physical simulation)

Key capabilities:
- Grid convergence verification (runGridConvergence.m) showing ~2nd-4th order accuracy
- Artificial dissipation for stability in under-resolved flows
- CFL-based adaptive time-stepping
- Performance-optimized sparse matrix fill for the pressure Poisson solve
- Regression check suite (runChecks.m)

The development log (memo) shows active research work from March 2026, focused on extending to curvilinear grids, fixing implicit solver boundary conditions, and adding periodic BCs for annular domains.




